# A PAD THROWS ITS SHADOW BEFORE IT LANDS (19_colossi `_warn`, DESIGN 5c). The
# straddling walker is staged ten world minutes before its foot comes down in
# this world's first tread; the player stands in its crater in the
# play view, on its floor, looking down. A breath and a half before the foot lands, the ground
# every pad will cover is marked and darkens as it comes; then it lands there.
#   TOUR_TIMEOUT=400 tools/tour.sh tours/colossi_warning.tour --seed=7 --place=tread0 --colossus=2@tread0-10 --hour=12 --weather=clear:0
zoom 34
await colossus_foot 30
near colossus_crater
until colossus_warned 30
wait 0.3
shot 00-the-shadow-falls with colossus_warned
wait 0.8
shot 01-darker-as-it-comes
until colossus_tread 10
wait 0.2
shot 02-it-lands-where-it-said
